tools/vendor/gscript.py
=======================

Origin: `tools/c3kit/formats/gscript.py` of the c3kit modding toolkit, part of the
tooling of the Cossacks 3 mod "Star Wars: Frontline Protocol" by the same author,
copied on 2026-09-28 from the installed copy of that mod
(source sha256 7184349e8000bcf36929ac78425cf5d4f556db6e9700339e2d07d18283fe5ff9,
39223 bytes). It is vendored so that this repository builds on a machine that
does not have that mod installed; `tools/hbuild.py` imports only this copy.

Modified: four comment/docstring phrases that cited the source project's own
rule numbers were reworded or dropped (module docstring lines 3 and 47-48, the
docstring of `natives()` line 157, the docstring of `balance()` line 587). No
code line was changed then (vendored copy sha256
6ee224635a043c0508c79d7791f4cfbac38a85392638ea1a74b76cc6d3298403, 39154 bytes).

Modified 2026-10-02: `_NAME_LINE` matches spaces and tabs within the line
instead of `\s`, which crosses line ends: on a section padded with empty lines
(the build lints each state at its own line numbers) the old pattern rescanned
the run of empty lines from every line start, 14 of a build's 19 seconds. Both
give the same name on all 379 wrapped inputs of a build and on every vanilla
.inc / .aix. Vendored copy now sha256
3acba68eefee71ef5e642fccb536c659efd4c455d2a2cabaa376e2afc01fe4f0, 39446 bytes.

Other references inside the file (`verify.py`, `tools/checks/gscript_check.py`,
`swfp.bytes_ops`, "conventions B8") point into the source project and are kept
as they were written; they explain where each rule was measured.


